Ciphertext lives here: age/<name>.age, created with `agenix -e`.

TRACKED ON PURPOSE, unlike secrets/ (which .gitignore excludes and which
holds plaintext staging). These files are age ciphertext and are safe to
commit to a public repo -- that is the entire point of the scheme.

They must also be tracked for a second, mechanical reason: this is a git
flake, and a git flake copies only TRACKED files into its store source.
An untracked .age file is invisible to evaluation, exactly as an untracked
feature directory is.
